# Realtime Auction Rule

Always follow `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/API_INTEGRATION.md`.

## Connection lifecycle

- Connect STOMP only when entering auction detail or bidding room.
- Disconnect on route unmount.
- Do not keep an app-wide idle websocket connection.

## Source of truth

- REST is authoritative.
- WebSocket is for fast UX and cache synchronization only.

## Event handling

- On `NEW_BID`, you may hot-patch Query cache with `queryClient.setQueryData`.
- After hot patch, refetch in background to confirm server state.
- If server state differs, Query replaces the temporary patch.

## Reconnect

- Use controlled backoff reconnect.
- After reconnect succeeds, refetch affected queries immediately.
- If websocket is unavailable, the UI may degrade gracefully but must not invent authoritative state.

## Time

- Countdown must use synchronized server time.
- Use offset logic from `docs/API_INTEGRATION.md`.
- Never trust raw local client time for auction countdown correctness.
